  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `add_tag`, and the public test now passes.\n\nThe problem was the default `tags=[]`. Python creates that list once, so every call that left out `tags` added to the same shared list. I changed the default to `tags=None` and create a new empty list inside the function when it's `None`.\n\nIf a caller passes their own list, it's still used as-is and gets the new tag added to it. I checked this directly: the record ends up holding the same list object that was passed in. `remove_tag` is unchanged.\n\nDONE: Replaced add_tag's mutable default `tags=[]` with `tags=None` plus a fresh list per call, so tags no longer leak between calls; public test passes.",
